 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T12:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**For a short walk or commute, you probably don’t need a mask if you’re otherwise healthy.** But Singapore is experiencing haze today, **17 October 2026**, and the official forecast is **Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy**. Avoid a long outing or strenuous exercise outdoors. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\n**Check the 1-hour PM₂.₅ reading for your area in the myENV app or on NEA’s haze site before you go**—that’s the measure Singapore advises using for an immediate decision, and I couldn’t reliably retrieve the live regional reading. If it’s **High**, older adults, pregnant people, and people with chronic heart or lung disease should avoid going out; if going out is unavoidable, a well-fitting **N95 or equivalent** can reduce exposure. Healthy people should avoid strenuous activity at that level. ([haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg/))",
